{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 18,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Through desire a man, having separated himself, seeketh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " intermeddleth with all wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fool hath no delight in understanding, but that his heart may reveal itself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the wicked cometh, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cometh also contempt, and with ignominy reproach.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The words of a man's mouth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " deep waters, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the well-spring of wisdom ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a flowing brook.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not good to accept the person of the wicked, to overthrow the righteous in judgment.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fool's lips enter into contention, and his mouth calleth for strokes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A fool's mouth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his destruction, and his lips ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the snare of his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The words of a tale-bearer ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as wounds, and they go down into the innermost parts of the belly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He also that is slothful in his work is brother to him that is a great waster.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The rich man's wealth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his strong city, and as a high wall in his own conceit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before destruction the heart of man is haughty, and before honor ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " humility.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that answereth a matter before he heareth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " folly and shame to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The spirit of a man will sustain his infirmity; but a wounded spirit who can bear?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The heart of the prudent getteth knowledge; and the ear of the wise seeketh knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man's gift maketh room for him, and bringeth him before great men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " first in his own cause ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "seemeth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " just; but his neighbor cometh and searcheth him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The lot causeth contentions to cease, and parteth between the mighty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A brother offended ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is harder to be won",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " than a strong city: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " contentions ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the bars of a castle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man's belly shall be satisfied with the fruit of his mouth; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with the increase of his lips shall he be filled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Death and life ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the power of the tongue: and they that love it shall eat the fruit of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoever",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " findeth a wife findeth a good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and obtaineth favor from the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The poor useth entreaties; but the rich answereth roughly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.18.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PRO.18.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that hath",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " friends must show himself friendly: and there is a friend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sticketh closer than a brother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
